    "lesson": {
      "title": "Trade tariffs and deadweight loss with imports",
      "instruction": "Adjust the per-unit tariff and world market price. Observe how higher tariffs protect domestic producers but tax consumers and shrink imports.",
      "explanation": "A tariff raises domestic price from P_w to P_dom. Domestic production expands and domestic consumption falls. The government collects tariff revenue (shaded purple), while production and consumption distortions create deadweight loss (shaded red)."
    },
